CAT = "caautoHev"; SEG = "HEV"
# RSOS 2023 MWA H: Diagnoses and repairs hybrid and electric vehicle (EV) systems (H-22, H-23)
Q = [
("What colour is used for high-voltage cables on hybrid and electric vehicles?",
 "Orange", ["Red", "Yellow", "Blue"],
 "Orange conduit and cables mark high-voltage circuits on hybrids and EVs, following an SAE convention. Treat any orange cable as live until you have proven it dead."),
("What must be done to high-voltage insulating gloves before each use?",
 "Air test them for leaks", ["Wash them in solvent", "Dust them with talc", "Test them with a megohmmeter"],
 "Trapping air in the glove and rolling the cuff shows pinholes or tears. They are worn with leather protectors and are also tested electrically at set intervals."),
("After the service disconnect is removed, why must the technician wait before working?",
 "For capacitors to discharge", ["For the coolant to drain", "For the 12 V battery to charge", "For the motor to stop spinning"],
 "The inverter capacitors can hold a dangerous charge after the battery is isolated. The maker gives a waiting time before the absence of voltage is checked."),
("When verifying zero voltage on a high-voltage circuit, what is done before and after the test?",
 "Check the meter on a known source", ["Zero the meter on the ohms range", "Measure the 12 V battery voltage", "Switch the meter to the amps range"],
 "Testing the meter on a known live source before and after proves it was working, so a zero reading means the circuit really is dead."),
("What does an insulation resistance tester check on a hybrid's high-voltage system?",
 "Leakage to the vehicle chassis", ["Battery state of charge", "Motor speed sensor output", "Inverter switching frequency"],
 "It applies a high test voltage between a conductor and the chassis and reads the resistance. A low reading shows insulation breaking down."),
("What does the high-voltage interlock loop do when a connector is unplugged?",
 "Opens the main contactors", ["Discharges the 12 V battery", "Sets the motor to generate", "Starts the cooling pump"],
 "The interlock is a low-voltage loop through high-voltage connectors and covers. If it opens, the system shuts the contactors and isolates the battery."),
("On most hybrids and EVs, what charges the 12 V battery while the vehicle is on?",
 "A DC-DC converter", ["A belt-driven alternator", "The onboard AC charger", "The regenerative brakes directly"],
 "A DC-DC converter steps the high-voltage battery down to charge the 12 V system. There is usually no alternator."),
("An EV will not power up even though the high-voltage battery is charged. What should be checked first?",
 "The 12 V auxiliary battery", ["The traction motor windings", "The DC fast charge port", "The HV battery coolant"],
 "The 12 V battery powers the modules and closes the main contactors. If it is flat, the high-voltage system cannot switch on."),
("What does DC fast charging bypass that Level 2 charging uses?",
 "The onboard charger", ["The battery management system", "The main contactors", "The HV battery cooling"],
 "Level 1 and 2 supply AC, which the onboard charger converts to DC. A DC fast charger supplies DC straight to the battery through the contactors."),
("What happens during regenerative braking?",
 "The motor acts as a generator", ["The friction brakes heat the battery", "The engine drives the wheels", "The inverter turns off"],
 "The drive motor is turned by the wheels and generates current that charges the battery, slowing the vehicle. Friction brakes add force when needed."),
("Why must only the specified oil be used in an electric A/C compressor?",
 "It must not conduct electricity", ["It must be thicker in winter", "It must match the engine oil", "It must contain a leak dye"],
 "An electric compressor's motor windings sit in the refrigerant oil. Non-conductive oil, often POE, keeps insulation resistance high; ordinary PAG can cause an isolation fault."),
("Why do brake rotors on hybrids and EVs often rust or seize?",
 "Regen does most braking", ["Their pads are softer", "They run hotter than normal", "The high voltage corrodes them"],
 "Light use of the friction brakes lets rust build on the rotors and slides. Many makers recommend cleaning and lubricating the brakes at set intervals."),
]
